{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098722-the-gematria-of-the-world-of-darkness","id":1098722,"title":"The Gematria of the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T03:22:00-07:00","id":1098722,"title":"The Gematria of the World of Darkness","content":"So, time for one of my weirder posts about the oWoD. If you play a Hermetic, a Tremere, or any other magick-y type, this post might be of interest to you. Before we get into the specific values, Gematria is the practice of computing numerical values for a name, place, or other word (or sentence) based on the letters of the word. I favour Hebrew gematria, but there are versions for English as well and for Greek. It has a long history in Western occultism and mysticism, and some neat stuff you might be able to use in your games. Non-Hebrew words have been transliterated or translated to the appropriate Hebrew word. More will come later - I'm a touch busy at the moment - so for now enjoy your long list of meaningless numbers.<br /> <br /> Our format is thus - WORD:VALUE/SOFIT VALUE || Interesting correlations<br /> <br /> NOD:60 || The upshot of many of the words here are that they are directly from the Hebrew, with long standing fascination to Kabbalists and qabalists. Huge reams of paper with seas of ink explore just what the gematric value of such words mean - and Nod is one of 'em if you want to dig deeper. Father's Brother, to purify, a stolen thing, curdled milk, to lament. So for a good example of how this shit might be useful in your games, the Malkavian who keeps screaming about the place of purification and thieves might very well be ranting about Nod.<br /> NAMARU:296<br /> HALAKU:75/535<br /> ASHARU:590<br /> ANNUNAKI:126/556<br /> NIBIRU:252<br /> LAMMASU:370<br /> RABISU:502<br /> CAINE:160/810<br /> ABEL:37<br /> HAQIM:145/705<br /> SET:69 or 700 || Varies depending on if you go by pronunciation or by the equivalent, Seth, from the Hebrew. I prefer the transliteration for its parallel to Mekhet.<br /> MEKHET:69<br /> LOZ:37 || So, first things - who the hell is Loz? Loz is a member of the Second or Third Generation and one of the Aralu. Potentially [Toreador], but not necessarily. Notably, the value is shared with Abel's. Correlations are to float, to leap, to be pure, to breathe, yehudia, to burn. I would personally use this to suggest that the Loz of the Aralu is in fact a tomb for Abel built long after the fact by a grieving Caine, but I'm like that and it may not suit your games.<br /> MALKAV:96<br /> MALKAVIAN:156/806<br /> LUCIAN:88/738<br /> RAVANA:256/906 || On a non-Gematria note, Days of Fire refers to Ravana as the Scion of the Greatest Thief. Scion can mean just descendant - but it more properly means the rightful heir or those of the first generation (or the firstborn exclusively) - which ties in nicely to the Ravnos story where Ravana is a direct childe of Caine.<br /> RAVNOS:316<br /> ARIKEL:250<br /> SAULOT:99 || 9 is an exciting number in its own right, as is 99. Broadly, 9 is the final step before a return to 1, so it has symbolism for the completion of cycles, etc. On a purely gematric note without additional numerological significance, 'Favor of God', 'a cutting off', 'mirror', and 'smitten by God', at least according to Heidrick.<br /> VENTRUE:271<br /> ILYES:100 || Shared with Ennoia, though Ennoia can be transliterated differently if you use the Greek gematria and can of course be transliterated quite differently in Hebrew. Ilyes is one of the names for the Brujah's true progenitor; shares a value with Strife (if not using sofits) and 'to deceive'.<br /> DRACIAN:262/912<br /> NINMUG:143<br /> ENNOIA:100/750 || With sofit, no longer shared with Ilyes. If one desires the greek value, it is 186. With sofit, 'to become dry', form or shape, species or kind.<br /> ENNOIA alternate:56 || This is one of the alternative means of transliteration.<br /> GANGREL:86 || Elohim. 'To be defective'. 'To befoul'. An abundance.<br /> NAMTARU:299<br /> NERGAL:283<br /> AL-MAHRI:276<br /> ABSIMILIARD:236<br /> TROILE:239 || Iron tools. Oddly enough, it almost seems like Ilyes and Troile should be swapped.<br /> BRUJAH:210 || Slaughter. To lay waste; to slay among them; to make hot.<br /> IRAD:284<br /> LAMECH:90<br /> LASOMBRA:602<br /> TREMERE:449<br /> ASHUR:511<br /> ENOCH:84<br /> ZILLAH:125<br /> JABAL:42<br /> ADAH:79<br /> TUBAL:47<br /> MEHUJAEL:95<br /> TALMAHERA:295<br /> BAALI:112<br /> AHRIMANE:296/946 || A value shared by Namaru, and potentially by Tal'mahe'ra.<br /> The One Giver:276 or 117/596 || Depends on if one takes the Hebrew word or transliterates. Tied to Al-Mahri in some unknown way.<br /> LILITH:480<br /> THE NEW LIGHT:519||The name of God after the revelation of the Angels to man.<br /> 9,009,909:...9999/36The number of Angels of the One Giver before the war. &quot;Repent; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will fight against them with the sword of my mouth.&quot;<br /> 6,006,666:...66666/30|The Loyal Angels. There are no particular associations for 66666, but when we reduce to 30 there are plenty.<br /> 3,003,302:...3332/11|The Rebels. &quot;Hear this, ye old men, and give ear, all ye inhabitants of the land. Hath this been in your days, or even in the days of your fathers?&quot;<br /> 1,001,101:...1111/4|The deaths caused by the rebels, and caused on them in turn. Glory - tifereth, and foundations - shathath. &quot;When they went from one nation to another, from <i>one</i> kingdom to another people;&quot;<br /> 2,002,201:...2221/7|The surviving rebels. &quot;But if ye shall still do wickedly, ye shall be consumed, both ye and your king.&quot;<br /> 2,002,204:...2224/10|The number of angels imprisoned in the pit. &quot;And let them be for lights in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth: and it was so.&quot;; &quot;But we are all as an unclean <i>thing</i>, and all our righteousnesses <i>are</i> as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 06-02-2017, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T09:57:46-07:00","id":1098806,"title":"","content":"Some of these numbers seem... very off to me.<br /> <br /> You seem to be using the absolute value method (though noted you have included the sofit method for a few. But there are ones that don't make sense. Abel, for instance, should be 37 in this method (5+2+30), since the original Hebrew name is actually Hebel. And the choice to count Irad as 274 instead of 284 doesn't seem consistent (treating the yud as a vowel and ignoring it) with Baali and Lilith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T21:43:37-07:00","id":1099016,"title":"","content":"I am a flawed creature with a limited grasp of Hebrew. It is known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T22:46:10-07:00","id":1099028,"title":"","content":"Moving to another post, a quick explanation of the 'why are these numbers here, Loomer. What do the numbers mean?!' (Just don't strap me in a chair and go all Black Ops on me, please.)<br /> <br /> The essential thinking of these correspondences for the kabbalist and qabalist and even the cabalist is that the underlying numerological formulas of names and events indicates their true and subtle natures or their place in a greater relational web of things. Take the proper Gematria for Cain - 160 - and a few options immediately leap out: 'To attack', for instance. But all the correspondences tie in, not just whatever seems best, and it is through synthesis and meditation that one might find the underlying reason - and that's where the long hours of meditation and thought come into play, because it's a real devil of a thing to try and do solo even if you aren't making basic mistakes with your Hebrew transliteration and dictionary like I just did.<br /> <br /> In theory, the end result of these correspondences is that you understand what ties them together and get a little closer to perceiving the true hidden warp and weave of the cosmos itself. In practical terms for your games, however, it's probably easier to use it for some of the following:<br /> - Cryptic passwords and research notes from the Hermetic mentor's diary<br /> - Secret identities (e.g. Set (though properly 217 as Seth) and Mekhet sharing a value would then suggest that either Set and Mekhet were one and the same, or that they bear some intimate connection)<br /> - Fate. The subtle webs of connection may reveal the ultimate fate or purpose of a character, NPC, or splat if you want to go that far.<br /> - Crazy shit for your NPCs or PCs to ramble off about.<br /> <br /> There are a number of further steps, but those can wait a long time before we even go near them. Things like the exact order of the letters in the Hebrew word or transliteration, the sums and reductions, and outright changing the values by fiddling with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:57:59-07:00","id":1099077,"title":"","content":"If you ever feel like poking me about this sort of thing feel free.<br /> <br /> Though, a really fun one for WtA focused characters that are struggling with a Abrahamic upbringing (or even a group of werewolves seeking to unify standard Garou beliefs with Abrahamic beliefs): Gaia's value is 18.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> To add to the cryptic password bit, anything thing with gematria is that there are more the one method of assigning values, many of which can be stacked together on the same text. You can construct passages that can layer 4-5 different value assignments into a giant ass puzzle of connections between words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T02:22:29-07:00","id":1099084,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms is not wrong. Trying to follow some of the more intricate gematric constructions of the various occultists and rabbis can be an exercise in mind bending even stronger than trying to make heads or tails of GURPS: Vehicles creation rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:35:41-07:00","id":1099366,"title":"","content":"GURPS Vehicles was easy enough, but no one really needed that level of detail, which is why they simplified things in 4e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:37:32-07:00","id":1099367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098722-the-gematria-of-the-world-of-darkness?p=1099084#post1099084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms is not wrong. Trying to follow some of the more intricate gematric constructions of the various occultists and rabbis can be an exercise in mind bending even stronger than trying to make heads or tails of GURPS: Vehicles creation rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know someone who could follow Gurps vehicles 3e... He also was able to make devices taht only functioned in his basement. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T21:16:04-07:00","id":1099385,"title":"","content":"I had many fond nights designing spacecraft with the system. Of course, that was when I was much younger and did not have a life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T21:22:12-07:00","id":1099386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098722-the-gematria-of-the-world-of-darkness?p=1099367#post1099367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know someone who could follow Gurps vehicles 3e... He also was able to make devices taht only functioned in his basement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though published for its third edition, it was technically GURPS Vehicles 2nd edition. Also, it wasn't that hard to follow. Just time consuming. I also had plenty of practice with GURPS Robots, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T23:05:21-07:00","id":1099400,"title":"","content":"Something requiring a certain amount of prior knowledge, a great deal of time and/or effort to understand and use, and which relies on an arcane series of formula and numbers with little if any obvious relation to what is actually being described until seen as a complete whole?<br /> <br /> Am I talking about Gematria or the Vehicles rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:03:08-07:00","id":1099527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098722-the-gematria-of-the-world-of-darkness?p=1099400#post1099400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something requiring a certain amount of prior knowledge, a great deal of time and/or effort to understand and use, and which relies on an arcane series of formula and numbers with little if any obvious relation to what is actually being described until seen as a complete whole?<br /> <br /> Am I talking about Gematria or the Vehicles rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Joke's on you - there isn't any prior knowledge that would help you with Vehicles! (^VVVVVVV^) Except at least getting to second year algebra in high school, but that's for when you want to intentionally maximize some part of construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}